A||N||12||pherder||Latest pictures of the HO Quad 4 ...||||1||
Z||000000||pherder||05-21-2000||07:57 PM||||The engine is back out and I am working on the wiring harness to find out why I have HOT AT ALL TIMES in the HOT in RUN, TEST, and START circuit.<P>Plus I will be routing the wiring MY WAY instead of the mess a company that does this for a living has it.<P>Let's see ... the red wire goes ... ?<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=21507762&Sequence=0"> <P>Also, while I had the engine out, I thought I would show a picture of the exhaust manifold, cat. converter and muffler in one shot!<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=21507759&Sequence=0"> <P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000001||redfiero||05-21-2000||08:35 PM||||Nice looking engine...especially the exhaust.  What company did you get your kit from?||||reg||1
Z||000002||pherder||05-21-2000||08:54 PM||||No kit, just self abuse ...<P>I have the install manuals from two different companies that I studied along with the factory service manuals for both the donor car (in this case for the wiring ... an 89 Grand Am) and of course, the 88 Fiero Coupe.<P>After following the wiring layout from one company as exactly as I could, i.e. using a 4 x 8 sheet of plywood and laying out the drawing of the wiring harness on the sheet, checking and rechecking the wires, I missed at least one (the reason for tearing it all apart ...) and the harness wouldn't fit very well so I decided to bite the bullet and re-do it all.  I have at least one loop of wires, approx. 1 foot long, that will be cut out and reattached (one wire at a time) to make the fit better.  It helps to have the engine sitting on the floor AND to have the measurements of where the wire bundles go (fender and to the center where the stock Fiero ECM goes.)<P>This is what I had planned to do in the beginning but I thought, why reinvent the wheel?  Just use the layout described in the install manual.  WRONG!  It just doesn't fit very well.  What I have planned and sort of have laid out, will make it a shorter harness and I will be sure that the correct wires go the correct places.  <P>The exhaust system is part The Fiero Store's "performance" exhaust system (the muffler and tips), a cat. conv. that I picked up from a Hot Rod shop, and the stock, cast iron exhaust manifold that I polished and then had treated/coated by HPC along with all the other pieces of the exhaust system.<P>Would I do another Quad 4? NO!  Would I try to talk someone out of trying to do one?  YES.<P>This is as hard a swap as any swap that includes a fuel injection system that was not stock on the Fiero.<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000003||lowCG||05-21-2000||09:24 PM||||Wow,I just came inside to get a break from sorting out the wires on my 3.4TDC swap,can't get away from it!<BR>I was advised that there could be a situation where the car won't shut off when the the key is turned off,just keeps running.<BR>Not sure of how it is exactly on the quad four donor car,but mine came with a relay to power the ignition functions(coils,ECM,injectors,sensors).<BR>I was advised to get rid of all the relays,including that one,but I'm not seeing any advantages in doing this,wouldn't it be better to keep all the higher powered wires in the engine compartment,and just fire the relay with a little wire?<P>The big purple(start)wire must be attached to something it shouldn't be to have power at all times.<P>I'm not sure how I'm going to separate the power distribution,but it will follow that of the donor car to take care and keep the circuits from feeding each other.<BR>This is the worst part of a swap,yet I'd rather do this than rebuild a motor with micrometers and guages,just to get another 20-30 hp.<BR>Keep me posted on any developements. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dan86gt3.8||05-22-2000||12:07 AM||||what tranny are you going with low cg?  I was in my moms monte carlo z34 again and wondered why I didn't get one.  It would be fun to rev it to 7k in a race.  I wonder what it would sound like to.  Man good luck with that harness, thats way out of my leauge!||||reg||1
Z||000005||lowCG||05-23-2000||02:03 AM||||Dan,my car came with a V6,and 5spd,am using that tranny,just found the last of my unidentified engine wires tonight,now to match them all together with the wires on my car.It took all weekend to identify and label each wire,now my next project will be to double check each wire again,after waiting a week for my headache to go away.<BR>I'll bet the 3.8 has a nice pull from lower revs,or in traffic though compared to the 3.4.||||reg||1
Z||000006||kevin||05-23-2000||10:24 AM||||I cannot understand why 'someone' who has ideas on making some money hasn't designed a well thought out kit for the Quad-4. I my mind the Quad-4 has many advantages over other engines for the Fiero. It just seems the initial puzzle on the correct methodology has yet to be steamlined. Keep at it! PLEASE!. I believe I can convince you that you can start a business helping us in our our Quad-4 rebuilds. I for one would be willing to exchange my money for your expertise. ||||reg||1
